# Font weights — tags and `<strong>` only

Do **not** use font-weight Tailwind utilities (`font-normal`, `font-medium`, `font-semibold`, `font-bold`, etc.) at call sites.

Adjust weight only by:

1. **Semantic text tags** — naked `h1`–`h6` (medium from `@layer base`)
2. **`<strong>`** — medium + `text-foreground` from `@layer base`

```tsx
// ✅
<p>Supporting copy</p>
<p><strong>HbA1c</strong></p>
<h6>Medications</h6>

// ❌
<p className="font-semibold">HbA1c</p>
<p className="font-medium">Title</p>
<span className="font-bold">…</span>
```

Primitive chrome may set weight only via `@apply` inside the component (co-located CSS / `@layer components`), never via call-site `className` weight utilities. Applied emphasis weight is **medium** (`font-medium` via `@apply`). Button and Badge stay regular by inheritance — do not add weight utilities on them.

See `design.md` → Typography → Font weights.
